{
  "uid": "trading-workflow-funnel",
  "title": "Trading \u2014 Workflow Funnel",
  "description": "How far work got, stage by stage. Counts only what the system actually emits; a stage with no metric shows as unavailable rather than as zero.",
  "tags": [
    "trading",
    "milestone-11"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-7d",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Reading this funnel honestly",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Each bar is **the number of runs that reached that stage**, not the number of candidates that survived it. The system does not emit a per-candidate counter at every stage, and inventing one from the counters it does emit would produce a plausible funnel that is not measured.\n\nWhere a stage shows **unavailable**, the metric has not been emitted \u2014 no run has happened, or telemetry is disabled. That is deliberately not rendered as `0`: *'nothing ran'* and *'a run selected nothing'* are different facts, and only the second is a statement about the market.\n\n`NO_TRADE` is a first-class outcome at every stage. A narrow funnel is the ordinary answer, not a fault."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "The opportunity funnel",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "bargauge",
